---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Case Studies | Product Thinking & Solutions Engineering">
<header class="page-intro">
  <p class="margin-note">Some problems I've spent time with.</p>
  <span class="eyebrow">Projects / Selected work</span>
  <h1>The things I've<br/><span class="accent">worked on.</span></h1>
  <p>Most of my work starts with a question someone needs answered. Sometimes the result is a product, sometimes a system behind the scenes, and sometimes a better way of measuring what's happening.</p>
</header>
<section class="section case-study" id="case-study" aria-labelledby="case-heading">
  <div class="section-row">
    <span class="eyebrow">01 / A closer look</span>
    <div class="case-main">
      <div class="case-intro">
        <div class="case-intro-copy">
          <span class="case-kicker">Valor Compounding Pharmacy · Customer operations</span>
          <h2 id="case-heading">Measuring more than the number of prescriptions typed.</h2>
          <p class="case-summary">The pharmacy's customer-care team handled calls, tickets, schedules, and prescriptions. But performance was being judged largely by prescription volume. I built a system that looked at the different work people were actually doing.</p>
          <div class="case-chips"><span>5 data sources</span><span>15+ KPIs</span><span>Role-based analytics</span></div>
        </div>
        <a class="case-cover" href="https://github.com/patilbp/performance-evaluation-metrics" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the performance evaluation project on GitHub">
          <img src="https://github.com/patilbp/performance-evaluation-metrics/assets/36761520/4397572a-bd15-4897-bda9-78edf25c6fcb" alt="Performance analytics project cover with miniature figures and capsules" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <span class="case-cover-caption">Project on GitHub ↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="case-workspace" data-case-tabs>
        <div class="case-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Read about the pharmacy performance analytics project">
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="case-tab-problem" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="case-panel-problem" tabindex="0" data-case-tab="problem"><span>01</span> Problem</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="case-tab-opportunity" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="case-panel-opportunity" tabindex="-1" data-case-tab="opportunity"><span>02</span> What I built</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="case-tab-solution" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="case-panel-solution" tabindex="-1" data-case-tab="solution"><span>03</span> What changed</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="case-tab-technical" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="case-panel-technical" tabindex="-1" data-case-tab="technical"><span>04</span> Another finding</button>
        </div>
        <div class="case-panels">
          <section role="tabpanel" id="case-panel-problem" aria-labelledby="case-tab-problem" data-case-panel="problem" tabindex="0">
            <span class="panel-eyebrow">What wasn't working</span>
            <h3>One number didn't tell the whole story.</h3>
            <p>Prescription volume alone missed the time people spent on calls, service requests, schedules, and other work. That made it difficult to assess different roles against the work each person was actually responsible for.</p>
          </section>
          <section role="tabpanel" id="case-panel-opportunity" aria-labelledby="case-tab-opportunity" data-case-panel="opportunity" tabindex="0" hidden>
            <span class="panel-eyebrow">The work</span>
            <h3>Five sources. More than fifteen KPIs.</h3>
            <p>I brought together calls, prescriptions, tickets, schedules, and employee data into a role-based performance analytics system. Different roles could be evaluated using targets that matched their responsibilities rather than one shared prescription count.</p>
          </section>
          <section role="tabpanel" id="case-panel-solution" aria-labelledby="case-tab-solution" data-case-panel="solution" tabindex="0" hidden>
            <span class="panel-eyebrow">The outcome</span>
            <h3>Clearer measures for the team.</h3>
            <p>Employee performance metrics improved 30% across Q1–Q2 2023. The system also supported workforce planning and more transparent employee appraisals.</p>
          </section>
          <section role="tabpanel" id="case-panel-technical" aria-labelledby="case-tab-technical" data-case-panel="technical" tabindex="0" hidden>
            <span class="panel-eyebrow">Another part of the job</span>
            <h3>Why were so many calls being missed?</h3>
            <p>I analyzed hourly, daily, weekly, and monthly call patterns and found a roughly 40% missed-call rate during peak hours. Extending Five9 history from three to twelve months helped guide staffing changes. Missed calls fell to 15% (a 62.5% relative reduction), and Zendesk tickets dropped from 120–150 to 40–50 a day (~67% reduction).</p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section" id="internal-products">
  <div class="section-row">
    <span class="eyebrow">02 / Products and systems</span>
    <div>
      <h2>A few more things I've built.</h2>
      <p>These examples come from my professional work. Not every internal system has a public demo, but the problems and outcomes are worth sharing.</p>
      <div class="project-list">
        <article>
          <div class="project-head"><span class="eyebrow">Black Book · Deployed</span><span class="project-status">Production product</span></div>
          <h3>BB Reporting Navigator</h3>
          <p>Our reporting dependencies were spread across hundreds of assets. I built a self-service place to trace what depends on what, which fields and metrics are affected, and what may change downstream.</p>
          <p class="project-fact">400+ assets · 960+ lineage relationships · 3,500+ governed fields · 20+ business metrics</p>
          <p>Based on recurring investigations, the estimated effort saved is around 300 hours per year.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div class="project-head"><span class="eyebrow">Black Book · In progress</span><span class="project-status">0→1 platform</span></div>
          <h3>Building our own analytics platform</h3>
          <p>I'm leading the architecture and technical research for an in-house Tableau replacement: a web app connected to our own semantic/data layer, security model, and deployment infrastructure. The work aims to reduce licensing costs and give teams more control over how analytics are built and delivered.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div class="project-head"><span class="eyebrow">Celandyne · Recruitment technology</span><span class="project-status">NLP &amp; matching</span></div>
          <h3>Helping recruiters compare résumés</h3>
          <p>I built an eight-stage Python NLP pipeline using PDF text extraction, preprocessing, TF-IDF, and cosine similarity. A KNN-based ranking step shortlisted the top 20 résumés for an opening. The design targeted matching results in under two seconds.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">03 / Data visualization</span><div><h2>Data visualization &amp; storytelling.</h2><p>My Tableau Public portfolio is a collection of interactive visual explorations and storytelling through data. It's one expression of how I make complex information easier to explore and understand.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/bhagyashri.patil" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore Tableau Public ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="https://www.tableau.com/blog/featured-authors-back-school-edition" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tableau Featured Author ↗</a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">04 / Elsewhere</span><div><h2>More of my work lives on GitHub.</h2><p>I keep some experiments and other code there, outside of the projects described above.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/patilbp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Browse GitHub ↗</a></div></div></div></section>
<section id="publications" class="section" aria-labelledby="publications-heading">
  <div class="section-row">
    <span class="eyebrow">05 / Publications</span>
    <div><h2 id="publications-heading">Published work.</h2><p>Earlier research on assistive technology, from my engineering background.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="publication-grid">
    <article class="publication">
      <span class="eyebrow">Publication / 2016</span>
      <h3>Camera-Based Assistive Text and Product Label Reading For Blind Person</h3>
      <p>International Journal of Innovative Research and Creative Technology (IJIRCT). Research into reading printed text and product labels using a camera to help people with visual impairments.</p>
      <a href="https://www.ijirct.org/papers/IJIRCT1601003.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read publication ↗</a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.case-main{min-width:0}
.case-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.5fr) minmax(255px,.9fr);align-items:center;gap:clamp(22px,3vw,46px)}
.case-intro-copy{min-width:0}
.case-cover{display:block;min-width:0;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;background:#e8e7f1;border:1px solid #e0e5ef;position:relative;transition:transform .2s ease}
.case-cover:hover{transform:translateY(-2px)}
.case-cover img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:1.5;object-fit:cover}
.case-cover-caption{position:absolute;bottom:0;left:0;right:0;padding:25px 14px 12px;background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(12,23,43,.75));color:#fff;font-size:.8rem;font-weight:800}
@media(max-width:800px){.case-intro{grid-template-columns:1fr}.case-cover{max-width:510px}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.case-cover{transition:none}}
.case-kicker,.panel-eyebrow{font-size:.74rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#626a78}
.case-main h2{max-width:880px;margin:12px 0 15px}
.case-summary{max-width:820px;margin:0;color:#60718a;font-size:1rem}
.case-chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin-top:19px}
.case-chips span{white-space:nowrap;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:650;color:#596370;padding:5px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #d5d8dc}
.case-workspace{border:1px solid #dfe7f2;border-radius:18px;background:#fff;margin-top:26px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 8px 30px #1c376408}
.case-tabs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:0;background:#f5f8fe;border-bottom:1px solid #dfe7f2}
.case-tabs button{border:0;border-bottom:3px solid transparent;padding:17px 10px 14px;background:transparent;color:#697994;font:750 .87rem "DM Sans",sans-serif;cursor:pointer;text-align:center;transition:background .15s,color .15s}
.case-tabs button span{color:#8494b5;font-weight:800;font-size:.7rem;margin-right:6px}
.case-tabs button[aria-selected="true"]{color:#253a6c;background:#fff;border-bottom-color:#555e6e}
.case-tabs button:hover{color:#284dad;background:#eef3fe}
.case-tabs button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #4c6ddc;outline-offset:-4px}
.case-panels{padding:clamp(22px,2.6vw,36px);min-height:260px}
.case-panels [hidden]{display:none!important}
.case-panels h3{font-size:clamp(1.3rem,2vw,1.7rem);margin:10px 0 13px}
.case-panels p{max-width:850px;font-size:.98rem;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 18px}
.case-panels ul{margin:6px 0 0;padding-left:20px;display:grid;gap:11px;color:#59697f;font-size:.96rem;line-height:1.6}
.panel-takeaway{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 17px;border-left:3px solid #626a78;background:#f5f8ff;padding:13px 17px;border-radius:0 9px 9px 0;color:#50627d;font-size:.89rem;line-height:1.6;max-width:850px}
.panel-takeaway strong{color:#263b66;flex:0 0 auto}
.panel-takeaway span{flex:1 1 400px}
@media(max-width:650px){.case-tabs{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.case-tabs button{padding:12px 7px;font-size:.8rem}.case-panels{min-height:0}.case-chips{gap:6px}.case-footer{align-items:flex-start}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.case-tabs button{transition:none}}
</style>
<script>
  const initializeCaseTabs = () => {
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-case-tabs]').forEach((workspace) => {
      if (workspace.hasAttribute('data-ready')) return;
      workspace.setAttribute('data-ready', 'true');
      const tabs = Array.from(workspace.querySelectorAll('[data-case-tab]'));
      const panels = Array.from(workspace.querySelectorAll('[data-case-panel]'));
      const activate = (tab, focus = false) => {
        const name = tab.getAttribute('data-case-tab');
        tabs.forEach((item) => {
          const active = item === tab;
          item.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(active));
          item.tabIndex = active ? 0 : -1;
        });
        panels.forEach(panel => { panel.hidden = panel.getAttribute('data-case-panel') !== name; });
        if (focus) tab.focus();
      };
      tabs.forEach((tab, index) => {
        tab.addEventListener('click', () => activate(tab));
        tab.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
          let next = index;
          if (event.key === 'ArrowRight') next = (index + 1) % tabs.length;
          else if (event.key === 'ArrowLeft') next = (index - 1 + tabs.length) % tabs.length;
          else if (event.key === 'Home') next = 0;
          else if (event.key === 'End') next = tabs.length - 1;
          else return;
          event.preventDefault();
          activate(tabs[next], true);
        });
      });
    });
  };
  initializeCaseTabs();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initializeCaseTabs);
</script>

<style>.accent{color:#4e5b6c}</style>
<style>
.publication-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:20px;margin-top:30px}
.publication{padding:28px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e1e8f2;border-radius:20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
.publication h3{margin:16px 0}
.publication p{flex:1}
.publication a{font-weight:800;font-size:.9rem;color:#4264cd}
.publication a:hover{text-decoration:underline}
@media(max-width:700px){.publication-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>

<style>

.accent{color:var(--sage);font-style:italic}
.case-kicker,.panel-eyebrow{color:var(--clay)}
.case-cover{border-radius:3px;background:var(--paper-deep);border-color:var(--line)}
.case-summary{color:#5c695d}
.case-chips span{color:var(--sage);border-bottom-color:#b8c5b5}
.case-workspace{background:#faf8f2;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:3px;box-shadow:none}
.case-tabs{background:#efeee5;border-bottom-color:var(--line)}
.case-tabs button{border-right:1px solid var(--line);color:#647064}
.case-tabs button:last-child{border-right:0}
.case-tabs button span{color:#8b9387}
.case-tabs button[aria-selected="true"]{background:#e2e9df;border-bottom-color:var(--sage);color:var(--sage-deep)}
.case-tabs button:hover{background:#e7ebe2;color:var(--sage-deep)}
.case-tabs button:focus-visible{outline-color:var(--sage)}
.case-panels h3{font:500 clamp(1.55rem,2.2vw,2.4rem)/1.2 Georgia,serif}
.case-panels ul{color:#566457}
.panel-takeaway{border-left-color:var(--sage);background:#eff2e9;color:#536454;border-radius:0}
.panel-takeaway strong{color:var(--sage-deep)}
.publication{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--paper-light);border-radius:3px}
.publication a{color:var(--sage);text-underline-offset:4px}
.publication h3{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:500}

</style>

<style>
.project-list{margin-top:30px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.project-list article{padding:27px 0 31px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.project-head{display:flex;gap:12px 20px;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:12px}
.project-status{font-size:.75rem;color:var(--muted)}
.project-list h3{font:500 clamp(1.55rem,2.1vw,2.15rem)/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:10px 0}
.project-list p{max-width:870px;margin:11px 0 0;font-size:.97rem}
.project-fact{color:var(--sage-deep)!important;font-weight:700;font-size:.88rem!important}
.publication-grid{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,850px)}
@media(max-width:700px){.project-head{align-items:flex-start}}
</style>
